A||||3||the need for speed||were the heck is the back up light switch at||||1||
Z||000000||the need for speed||09-20-2000||12:11 PM||||I have an 87 gt 5 speed, took the shifter dash tray/ash trays out but do not see a switch of any kind.also looked on the tranny but agin do not see anything, bought a back up light switch it looks kind of like a triangle with a hole in one end, the salesman said that the 87 4cyl and v6 are the same thing i see nothing like what he sold me.the reverse lights have not worked since I got the car. I read some past post that said that the switch was there problem. the bulbs are fine,they said that they could push the stick left or right in reverse and hold it and  there lights would work, I tryed this and it does not work. So were is the back up light switch at????   ||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||09-20-2000||12:35 PM||||First, basic stuff - ignition has to be on for BU lights.  On the 5-speed, it has to be shifted fully into reverse for the lights to come on.  Also - check your fuses before you bother trying to replace the BU switch.    <P>On 4-speed Muncies, the BU switch is in the console.  It only detects the side-to-side motion of the shifter - when properly adjusted, the BU lights come on as soon as you move the stick into the reverse gate.<P>I think your BU light switch is in the trans., not in the console.  If it's a 1987GT and everything's original equipment, it's a 5-speed Getrag, which is <B>not</B> the same as the 5-speed used in the 4-cyl models.<P>Sounds like you need a new parts guy.  <P> <p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 09-20-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000002||StuGood||09-21-2000||12:40 AM||||Just looked at my 1987 GT w/5-speed Getrag.  The back-up light switch screws into the top of the transaxle, near the shift shaft & levers (where the shift cables attach).<P>The switch has 2 black wires going to a pigtail connector.  There, it plugs into the car's wiring harness.  The 2 harness wires are: light green, and navy blue.<P>Note: my car has a newer-than-1987 Getrag, so it's <B>possible</B> some of the wiring was altered, when the new tranny went in (?).<P>Hope this helps   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">       <p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 09-21-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Indiana_resto_guy||09-21-2000||06:54 PM||||Stugood is correct, ALL 5-speed reverse light swithches are in the case.||||reg||1
